A||||13||GodSend||Shipping things to Canada?||||5||
Z||000000||GodSend||03-18-2001||11:19 AM||||I hope I am in the right area.  These are parts (mostly stereo) for my 87' GT.<P>CUrrently my Bro has a few stereo items in California he would like to ship me for my Birthday (to the TOronto area).  These are both gifts, and I shouldent have to pay any duties on them.  <P>Are there forms which he needs to fill out for these items, or is writing "GIFT" on the outside of the box good enough? <P>Does anyone have any advice for UPS vrs USPS (i am not in a super rush, but also dont want to wait 3+ weeks)....<P>Thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||voyagerspe||03-18-2001||11:40 AM||||hi<BR>there are duties on electronics.  however there are not duties on car parts.  Just declare the items as car parts and you wont have any problems.(and you not lying because they are car(electronic) parts)||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||03-18-2001||11:42 AM||||Steve aka (DaRkLoRD) Would know this! I have shipped him parts USPS I'll be shipping him another package soon, and was going to ship it UPS? I'm not sure of the price difference of the two. The ship time 2-3 weeks is the same. I'm sure Steve will reply to this.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000003||overlord||03-18-2001||01:14 PM||||i received my BRA from the states, and i had to pay duty on it......and thats not electronics.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||03-18-2001||01:49 PM||||ive sent quite a few things out to canada. all i did was go to the post office, fill out a customs claim form stating what was in there and the value, and paid my shipping costs. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||03-18-2001||02:29 PM||||customs charges are a pain in the a$$. those quarter panels cost me $45 to get.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||billfredmike24||03-18-2001||09:32 PM||||Got a pioneer cd deck and some 4 x 10's from autotoys,  cost me $110 to get them from the ups guy, and i already payed shipping when i ordered the stereo.  Had to pay the 15% tax (gst ,pst) then the price for customs fee.<BR>Bought some rims from tsw, were shipped fedex and payed nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierosound||03-18-2001||11:23 PM||||If at all possible I AVOID UPS!!!  They'll charge you $38 "brokerage fee" for clearing customs, PLUS any taxes that may be due.  I always try to get items sent through the mail.  Post Office handling fees are only $5 plus taxes due.||||reg||11
Z||000008||DXR_DAD||03-18-2001||11:40 PM||||So Steve, How do you want me to ship the other package????<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000009||terryk||03-19-2001||12:13 AM||||If it can go post, do it. Everytime I've shipping UPS into Canada it took forever. Avoid UPS into Canada!<P>It's my understanding that Canadian Post delivers it anyway.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroLisa||03-19-2001||08:23 AM||||Why have I never had to pay these taxes and customs crap...I've sent things through the post office a couple times, and postage for a small box usually only runs me about 4 bucks total.||||reg||1
Z||000011||DXR_DAD||03-19-2001||11:56 AM||||Lisa I think they pay it on the pick-up end.<BR>Before you pick it up you must pay the customs charges and tax!  <P>DXR_DAD ||||reg||1
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||03-19-2001||03:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DXR_DAD:<BR><B>Lisa I think they pay it on the pick-up end.<BR>Before you pick it up you must pay the customs charges and tax!  <P>DXR_DAD </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, that's right. I've heard fedex is better than UPS, but overall I think regular mail is the cheapest. The smaller the package the lower the cost, also. I assume the JC Whitney package is going to come already in a box? just slap a new label on it I guess, or qrap it in brown paper and put a label on..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||kornholio||03-19-2001||11:30 PM||||If it's a gift, it has to include a card or something stating that it is a gift.  For gifts, only $60 is tax free.  They tax the excess of $60.<P>I bought an amp from the states last year.  UPS charged me a brokerage fee and taxes of $60 (if I remember correctly).  The amp only cost $130 US.  I try to avoid UPS if I can.  They're #@$%'n crooks.<P>I also bought a remote starter from the states and shipped it by USPS.  The guy marked it as a gift and I didn't even have to pay any taxes.  It was a $90 value.||||reg||1
